---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="The cookies and similar technologies used on Davis Weather Station, and how to manage them."
>
  <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. Similar technologies include local
    storage, session storage, pixels, and browser fingerprinting. They can help a site function, remember
    preferences, or measure usage.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Our approach</h2>
  <p>
    We keep tracking to a minimum. The Site does <strong>not</strong> use advertising cookies, third-party analytics,
    social-media pixels, or cross-site behavioural advertising. We do not sell or share personal information for
    advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Strictly necessary cookies</h2>
  <p>
    These cookies and storage are required for the Site and its security features to work. They do not require
    consent where they are strictly necessary.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Typical duration</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Hosting and security provider</td>
        <td>Security, load balancing, bot mitigation, and network performance.</td>
        <td>Session to 1 year, depending on the cookie.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Bot protection</td>
        <td>Distinguishes people from automated submissions on the quote form.</td>
        <td>Session to 1 year, depending on the challenge.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Our security provider may set cookies or use similar storage as part of its security and bot-protection services. Those
    cookies are controlled by that provider and are subject to its own policies. We do not control the exact
    duration or contents of third-party cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete or block cookies through your browser settings. The exact steps vary by browser; look for
    “Privacy”, “Cookies”, or “Site data” in your browser’s settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may prevent
    the quote form or security checks from working.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we do not use advertising cookies, there is no advertising opt-out to manage on this Site.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    Some browsers send a “Do Not Track” signal. Because we do not track users across sites or use advertising
    analytics, we do not currently respond differently to these signals.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy if our use of cookies changes. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page shows
    the latest revision.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about cookies? Contact us at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a> or through the{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
